## Verdict

`ACCEPT`

RB-01 is closed at design-review level.

The bounded Local repair directly addresses the only remaining blocker from the
final external adversarial review without reopening settled architecture or
introducing a parallel protocol, owner, registry, runtime, receipt owner,
schema, state machine, or fifth implementation path.

Acceptance here closes design review only. It grants no implementation,
packet-refresh, public-export, commit, push, provider, deployment, or production
authority.

## RB-01 Closure Check

| Check | Result | Evidence from revised design | Conclusion |
|---|---|---|---|
| Receipt machine-binds exact return-manifest SHA-256 | `PASS` | The Local reconciliation binding records `returnManifestSha256`; the referenced PASS receipt must expose `validatedReturnManifestSha256`; Local reconciliation requires exact equality. | Exact manifest binding is explicit and machine-checkable. |
| Receipt records `validatedProtocolVersion: 1.2.0` | `PASS` | The receipt contract explicitly requires `validatedProtocolVersion: 1.2.0`; Local reconciliation checks equality to that protocol version. | A candidate-unaware or wrong-protocol PASS cannot satisfy typed reconciliation. |
| Receipt records `validatedCandidateContractVersion: 1` | `PASS` | The receipt contract explicitly requires `validatedCandidateContractVersion: 1`; Local reconciliation checks it against `externalReturnBinding.candidateContractVersion`. | Strict candidate semantics actually enforced are now part of the evidence relation. |
| Receipt requires `status: PASS` | `PASS` | The receipt contract includes `status: PASS`; Local reconciliation explicitly checks `receipt.status == PASS`. | Receipt identity alone is insufficient; successful validation is required. |
| Local reconciliation verifies all receipt-binding relations | `PASS` | The revised contract compares manifest hash, candidate-contract version, PASS status, protocol version, and validated candidate-contract version. | The former “two independent hashes” ambiguity is removed. |
| Legacy or candidate-unaware PASS is insufficient | `PASS` | The revised design states that a legacy/candidate-unaware PASS remains historical evidence but cannot open typed Local reconciliation; the compatibility section repeats that candidate-unaware validators cannot produce sufficient typed evidence. | The residual BF-03 compatibility hole is closed. |
| Requested negative tests remain in the four-path delta | `PASS` | The focused-test responsibility includes wrong-manifest receipt, mismatched candidate-contract version, legacy-validator PASS, malformed discriminator, silent legacy promotion, contamination, reference integrity, and authority widening. | RB-01 failure modes are represented in the future test surface. |
| No new receipt owner, schema, registry, protocol, or fifth path | `PASS` | The design retains the existing four paths only and explicitly states no new schema file is justified. Receipt binding remains within the existing representation/validator/test ownership. | The repair preserves the existing-owner architecture. |
| Optional source-ref set-equality refinement is safe | `PASS` | The external-value candidate now requires `set(sourceRefs) == set(sourceLocations[].sourceRef)`. | Duplicate representations cannot drift or credit a source lacking an exact location. |
| Every new 1.2 producer emits the discriminator, including empty candidate arrays | `PASS` | The compatibility section requires every new 1.2 producer to emit `candidateContractVersion: 1`; absent discriminator + empty array is legacy-read compatibility only. | Producer semantics are deterministic while preserving 1.1 read compatibility. |

RB-01 closure relation is now:

```text
externalReturnBinding.returnManifestSha256
  ==
receipt.validatedReturnManifestSha256

externalReturnBinding.candidateContractVersion
  ==
receipt.validatedCandidateContractVersion

receipt.status
  ==
PASS

receipt.validatedProtocolVersion
  ==
1.2.0

receipt.validatedCandidateContractVersion
  ==
1
```

This is sufficient to prove, at the proposed design-contract level, that the
typed Local reconciliation is opened only by a PASS receipt for the exact
manifest under the strict candidate-aware 1.2 semantics.

The stable candidate identity remains:

```text
(returnManifestSha256, candidateId)
```

No globally allocated candidate ID or candidate registry is required.

## Remaining Blocking Findings

`NONE`

No new blocker was introduced by the RB-01 repair.

The optional refinements requested by the closing prompt are both safely
resolved:

1. exact set equality between `sourceRefs` and
   `sourceLocations[].sourceRef` is now normative for external-value candidates;
2. every new protocol-1.2 producer must emit
   `candidateContractVersion: 1`, including when the candidate collection is
   empty.

The following previously settled decisions remain intact:

- reuse `cvf.external-agent-round-trip`;
- protocol target `1.2.0`;
- retain `cvf.externalAgentReturn.v1`;
- dual-reader preservation for historical 1.1 evidence;
- two mutually exclusive candidate provenance lanes;
- deterministic parent-return/candidate join;
- Local Agent verifies current CVF overlap;
- Operator selection does not grant implementation authority;
- `WORK_ORDER_AUTHORIZED` remains rejected;
- no new collaboration protocol or profile;
- no new verified-map registry;
- no global collaboration state machine;
- no new runtime;
- no new truth owner;
- no new receipt owner;
- no new authority owner;
- no new schema file;
- four-path future implementation delta only.

